---
import CardCollection from '../components/CardCollection.astro';
import ChaosPromo from '../components/ChaosPromo.astro';
import Site from '../layouts/Site.astro';
import GovernmentNote from '../components/GovernmentNote.astro';
import { governmentContext, governmentMunicipalityIds, governmentSource } from '../lib/governance/index.ts';
const councils = governmentMunicipalityIds.map(id=>governmentContext(id)!).sort((a,b)=>a.municipality.name.localeCompare(b.municipality.name));
---
<Site title="Council governments & coalition history" description="Recorded South African municipal administrations, coalition members and source notes from MISTRA, with coverage through 28 February 2026.">
<div class="page-top"><p class="eyebrow">Before & after the 2026 election</p><h1>Council governments</h1></div>
<ChaosPromo/>
<details class="card government-method"><summary>Coverage & comparison notes</summary><p>80 municipalities · 175 recorded administrations</p><p>These records cover November 2021 to <strong>28 February 2026</strong>. They are historical context, not a live government register. Party roles, seats and officeholders describe each administration at formation; later changes may appear in its notes. “Active” means active at MISTRA’s cutoff.</p><p>Members and outside supporters are listed separately. A seat majority does not confirm a coalition agreement. Missing records do not establish a single-party government. District councils are outside this dataset’s coverage.</p><p>Our 2026 comparisons show the seats of the recorded founding members as a hypothetical combination. Estimates remain estimates, and completed reporting does not mean an official declaration. A confirmed government change requires separately sourced administrations before and after the election.</p><p>Published 7 October 2026 · MISTRA 2026 edition, version 1.0. Known issues from its release notes are shown with affected records.</p><div class="links"><a href={governmentSource.download}>Download the original data ↗</a><a href={governmentSource.codebook}>Codebook ↗</a><a href={governmentSource.releaseNotes}>Release notes ↗</a><a href="/api/v1/governments">Counted API →</a></div></details>
<details class="card government-method"><summary>Majorities & earlier elections</summary><p>We also record single-party administrations when municipal documents establish who formed the government. Buffalo City’s 2024/25 annual report records an ANC-led government following the 2021 election; the IEC allocation gives the ANC 61 of 100 seats. These separately sourced facts are not part of MISTRA’s coalition dataset or its licence.</p><p>Elsewhere, a complete 2021 IEC allocation can show the previous council’s outright majority. We label this as an election outcome, rather than evidence of uninterrupted government. Vote-share charts on municipality, province and national pages compare the same ballot basis over time and identify provisional 2026 points.</p></details>
<section aria-labelledby="recorded-councils"><h2 id="recorded-councils">Recorded administrations</h2><CardCollection id="government-cards" label="councils"><div class="government-directory" data-card-grid>{councils.map(c=><article class="card"><h3><a href={`/2026/places/${c.municipality.slug}#government`}>{c.municipality.name}</a></h3><GovernmentNote context={c}/></article>)}</div></CardCollection></section>
<details class="card government-method"><summary>Sources & reuse</summary><p>{governmentSource.attribution}</p><p><a href="https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/">CC BY 4.0 ↗</a> applies to MISTRA’s original coalition coding. Underlying IEC seat figures and municipal identifiers retain their original terms; this is not a blanket open licence for every field. We have not imported ACCORD’s database, financial indicators or population figures.</p><p>Counted normalises dates, matches municipal codes to its directory, expands party labels and attaches source issue flags. It preserves original notes and inaugural values. Our comparisons are Counted’s calculations; they do not imply MISTRA endorsement.</p><a href={governmentSource.licenceUrl}>Licensing and third-party sources ↗</a></details>
</Site>
<style>
.government-method{margin:12px 0;padding:8px 18px}.government-method>summary{min-height:44px;align-content:center;font-size:14px}.page-top{display:block}.page-top>p:last-child{margin-top:16px;color:var(--muted)}.government-method p{font-size:14px;line-height:1.8;max-width:900px}.government-directory{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(auto-fit,minmax(min(100%,260px),1fr));gap:16px;margin:24px 0 36px}.government-directory h3{margin:0;font-size:18px}.government-directory .card{padding:20px}.page-top>p{line-height:1.7}
</style>

